  ('anglais9e', $q${"type": "qcm", "question": "Text: \"Living in a big city has good advantages and disadvantages. Life in the city can be expensive, and there are often pollution and traffic. But many people like cities because they are convenient and full of opportunities. One big advantage is public transportation. Buses, trains, and subways help people move around easily. They also reduce traffic and make travel cheaper because you don't need a car or parking. Another benefit is healthcare. Cities have many hospitals and clinics, and some are open all day and night. City life also offers fun and social activities. There are many places to meet people, enjoy nightlife, and experience different cultures.\"\n\nIdentify the transportation that helps people move around easily in a big city.", "choices": ["hospitals", "buses and trains", "parking lots", "shopping centers"], "answer": 1, "answer_text": null, "explain": "« Buses, trains, and subways help people move around easily. »", "chapter_id": null, "year": 2026, "session": "Texte modèle mai 2026", "source": "MENFP – Bureau national des examens d'État, texte modèle 9e AF 2026"}$q$::jsonb),
